{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_2.march","start_line":7,"start_col":17,"end_line":7,"end_col":32,"message":"`greet` takes a `Cap(IO.Console)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `greet` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":7,"start_col":11,"end_line":7,"end_col":34,"text":""},{"kind":"replace","start_line":13,"start_col":10,"end_line":13,"end_col":15,"text":""}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_2.march","start_line":12,"start_col":16,"end_line":12,"end_col":23,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":9,"end_line":12,"end_col":24,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":25,"end_line":12,"end_col":25,"text":"needs IO "}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_2.march","start_line":13,"start_col":10,"end_line":13,"end_col":13,"message":"`greet` needs console access, but `cap` is the full IO capability.","code":"cap_mismatch:IO.Console","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_2.march","start_line":13,"start_col":4,"end_line":13,"end_col":23,"message":"`greet` needs `Cap(IO.Console)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_2.march","start_line":12,"start_col":10,"end_line":12,"end_col":13,"message":"`cap` was bound here as `Cap(IO)`"}],"notes":["`IO` contains `IO.Console`, but a capability is never narrowed implicitly.","help: capability values were retired; remove the parameter and this argument (see the `cap_param_retired` error on the parameter)."],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
